Linux-specific additions
-------------------------

Functionality original to this branch (not part of the upstream
macOS/Windows project) includes, among other work:

- Linux desktop integration via Avalonia, XDG autostart, Linux tray
  behavior, and a user-level desktop launcher and installer.
- Wayland global hotkey detection via an evdev backend, with XDG-portal
  and focused-only fallbacks, plus per-desktop shortcut writers
  (GNOME, KDE, Hyprland, Sway) and a one-click auto-setup flow.
- CUDA GPU support for the bundled whisper.cpp transcription engine on
  compatible NVIDIA systems.
- A local HTTP API and installable CLI for desktop automation.
- Per-app text-insertion strategies and smart Auto insertion tuned for
  Linux browsers, terminals, and Wayland/X11 sessions.
- Linux transcription cleanup pipeline, profile style presets,
  developer-safe formatting, voice command suffixes, and IDE file
  references.
- Correction suggestions with optional auto-learning, extended
  dictionary/snippet metadata, and additional dashboard metrics.

This list is illustrative, not exhaustive; see the README and the
per-release notes under docs/releases/ for details. Additional
Linux-specific functionality is ongoing.


